casions or if your budget allows. The staff has always been helpful with suggestions and never scoffs at my price limitations. They also have champagne and liquor. I highly recommend The Wine Seller for your wine needs!"},{"business_id":"qBD4MOO_kWoTTVkDQbDEag","review_id":"hygQciZns5EB-IwYbIMPrg","date":"2011-02-14T21:57:34","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9416279792785645,"text_excerpt":"Nice place which happens to be easy walking distance from my fiancee's place so it s generally my go-to shop. There are a few bottles at very low price points and a few on the higher end but most seem to be in the $15-50 range and the folks at the shop will help steer you toward whatever you want. Given the small space and an entire wall devoted to [good] beer & liquor you won't find the largest wine selection in the world at The Wine Seller but they seem to pick good wines at every price and style so you're unlikely to go wrong. As with any small brick & mortar shop you'll pay a few dollars more than an online retailer but you also don't have to pay shipping and you're helping keep good ..."},{"business_id":"qBD4MOO_kWoTTVkDQbDEag","review_id":"Cfymry9wATsHuQXXuVmdSg","date":"2010-10-01T21:38:34","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9405050873756409,"text_excerpt":"I'd like to say always always follow Jen L.'s advice as she has yet to steer me wrong (your rock girl!) ... BUT- the Wine Seller is a GREAT place to buy CHEAP bottles! I first thought that it might only have some upscale prices and that i'd walk out empty handed or with something for a special occasion but I really think that the Wine Seller has wines for every price range. I happen to love Spanish Tempranillo's and I appreciate the variety offered here. They take the time to make sure that they know about each bottle and that they are hand chosen. I found a Tempranillo for $7, $12, and more than $20. Totally affordable! I did not, however, find any two-buck-chuck here. Check out the very..."}],"visual":[{"busin